  <div class="section reveal">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-label">FAQ</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Questions Answer Engines Ask</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Can my bank correct my counterparty’s address for me?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>No. Under EPC §3.2 a payment service provider may correct its own customer’s address but must pass counterparty addresses through unchanged — so a corporate must fix beneficiary data at source.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Who is liable if a payment is rejected for an unstructured address?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>The originator. From 15 November 2026, CBPR+ and SEPA reject non-compliant payments at the network, and the liability sits with whoever assembled the payment.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Does ioNova ARS work inside SAP, Oracle, Kyriba, GTreasury and ION?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>Yes — it deploys as a sidecar via REST, SFTP, JDBC and File Upload, with no core replacement.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">How many addresses can I remediate at once?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>Up to 10,000 addresses per call for batch master-data clean-up.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">How fast can corporate treasury go live?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>Typically 3–4 weeks end to end, with the sandbox live and returning resolved addresses within about two days.</p></div></div>
      </details>
      <details class="faq-item">
        <summary class="faq-q">Is the correction auditable?<svg class="faq-chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9" /></svg></summary>
        <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner"><p>Yes — every correction is deterministic and cites a regulatory rule_source, so the same input always produces the same output.</p></div></div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>

